## Lore

*Quatoria* is an archaic wolfen word meaning **officer of the Law**. In the
pre-industrial Wolfen Empire they were law enforcement, and in remote country a
Quatoria was marshal, judge, jury, executioner and grave digger in one person.
When the Empire went to the stars they became the law sent to its most remote
and unruly corners, where they would be the only symbol of it for a very long
way.

To make sure they survived that, they were rebuilt. Bone implants, artificial
muscle and wired reflexes turned them into super-powerful creatures who still
look like wolfen, with most of their internal organs and bones replaced by
machinery. The implants make them superb spies and detectives - but the hardware
is secondary to the training and indoctrination that comes with it.

## Dedicated, and some would say fanatical

Quatoria have little sympathy for the criminal element. Where a *dead or alive*
option exists, most prefer to bring them back dead: it saves the taxpayer a
trial. Abuses happen, and innocent people have been killed by overzealous
Quatoria - and since they mostly work the lawless corners of the Three Galaxies,
those abuses often go unreported and unnoticed.

Since the Wolfen Empire joined the CCW, every Quatoria is a Bonded Deputy with
authority across all the Consortium''s planets. They routinely pursue criminals
past its borders anyway, where the only backing they have is their guns and
their fists.

## GM Notes

Quatoria often work undercover as pirates, smugglers or bounty hunters. Some
have built deep underworld contacts and real friendships in the seedier circles
of the CCW and the independent worlds, which is a complication the class is
written to have rather than a flaw in it.

Alignment is usually good or selfish. Some have become aberrant, and a few
renegades are pure evil.
